            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "3 ways Buffett's successor can keep Berkshire growing",
            "description": "<p>Warren Buffett will officially step down as CEO of Berkshire Hathaway (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/BRK-B\">BRK-B</a>, <a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/BRK-A\">BRK-A</a>) at the end of the year, with vice chairman Greg Abel set to replace him. The Glenview Trust Company chief investment officer, Bill Stone, explains what Abel should (and should not) do as he readies to take the helm of the conglomerate.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more <a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-catalysts/\">Market Catalysts</a>.</p>",
